### Intro: Krista's office (character creation frame) + apartment.

=== intro_session
-- start
ELLIOT (V.O.): Hello, friend. I'm going to talk to you, because I don't talk to anyone else. Not really. Not even her.
> Krista's office. Rain on the window, the radiator ticking, a box of tissues angled toward your chair like an accusation.
KRISTA: You came. Two weeks in a row. I'm going to pretend that's normal so you don't get spooked.
ELLIOT: I said I'd come.
KRISTA: You say a lot of things, Elliot. Last week you said the sleeping was better. Then you fell asleep in the waiting room. How is it, really?
-- feel
ELLIOT (V.O.): She wants a reading. A number for the inside of my head. You pick. I don't trust my instruments.
* "It's fine. Everything's quiet." -> feel_cold ! set tone=cold
* "I'm angry. All the time. At people I've never met." -> feel_angry ! set tone=angry ; stab -5
* "Tired. Not the kind sleep fixes." -> feel_numb ! set tone=numb
-- feel_cold
KRISTA: Quiet. You say that the way people say the house is quiet right before they mention the noise in the attic.
-> intake_prompt
-- feel_angry
KRISTA: At people you've never met. That's specific. Most people are angry at someone they know. You picked strangers. I'd like to know which ones, someday.
-> intake_prompt
-- feel_numb
KRISTA: Okay. I'm writing that down, and I'm underlining it, and you're going to pretend you didn't see me do that.
-> intake_prompt
-- intake_prompt
KRISTA: New practice policy. Everyone fills this out every six months. Strengths, habits, what you're good at, what you'd change. Be honest. Or at least be interesting.
ELLIOT (V.O.): A form. She thinks a form can hold me. Fine. I'll give her the parts of me that fit in boxes.
-> END

=== intro_after
-- start
KRISTA: Thank you. That's more than you've given me in a month.
ELLIOT: Don't get used to it.
KRISTA: I never do. One more thing, and then I'll let you go. You keep saying 'at night.' 'I do things at night.' 'I can't sleep because of what I do at night.' What do you do at night, Elliot?
ELLIOT (V.O.): I read people. Their mail, their messages, the things they think they deleted. I know her boyfriend's real name. I know her mother's maiden name. I know what she searched for at two in the morning last Tuesday. I could tell her. I never will.
* "Maybe next time." -> soft ! trust krista 1
* "I don't sleep. I read. That's all." -> deflect
* [SPEECH 30] "If I told you, you'd have to do something about it. So let's not." -> honest | deflect
-- soft
KRISTA: Next time. You've been saying that since March. One of these weeks I'm going to hold you to it.
-> out
-- deflect
KRISTA: You read. Okay. I'm a therapist, Elliot. 'I read' is what people say when they don't want me to ask what.
-> out
-- honest
KRISTA: ...That's the most honest thing you've ever said in this room. And I'm not going to ask what it means. Which probably says something about me, too.
! trust krista 2 ; set krista_suspects
-> out
-- out
KRISTA: Go home. Eat something that didn't come out of a machine. Talk to a neighbor. Sleep. That's your homework.
ELLIOT (V.O.): Homework. Fine. Home is two blocks east. My computer has been running all day, and I left it on a black screen this morning. I'm almost sure I did.
! quest mq_hello 10
-> END

=== apt_qwerty
-- start
ELLIOT (V.O.): Qwerty. My fish. He doesn't judge me. Or he judges me constantly and can't do anything about it. Either way, he's the only one who's never lied to me.
* Feed him. -> feed
* Just watch. -> watch
* "You ever think about getting out of there, Qwerty?" -> escape
-- feed
ELLIOT (V.O.): The flakes hit the water. He rises. Simple needs, simple joys. I envy the little bastard.
! trust krista 0
-> END
-- watch
ELLIOT (V.O.): He does a lap. Then another. A tiny loop, forever, in a box he can see through but never leave. I know the feeling.
-> END
-- escape
ELLIOT (V.O.): He doesn't answer. Fish never do. But I like to think, if he could, he'd say: the glass isn't the problem. It's that you keep feeding the thing that keeps you in.
! stab 2
-> END
